WEBVTT

00:00:00.013 --> 00:00:05.387
Postgres also supports a setting called security invoker for views.

00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:14.007
With this setting, Postgres checks access to the underlying tables using the permissions of the person who is running

00:00:14.007 --> 00:00:19.292
the view. This matters in real systems with multiple roles and permission levels.

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:24.552
For this course, focus on the idea: the view definition and the permission model are connected,

00:00:24.552 --> 00:00:31.053
and both need to be tested in the environment where the view will actually be used.
